description:
Build an in-memory repository that any entity type can use, with validation rules, change events, transactions and paging. It brings together generics, delegates and events, exceptions, `IDisposable` and iterators.

```csharp
public interface IEntity { int Id { get; } }

public record Product(int Id, string Name, decimal Price) : IEntity;

public record Change<T>(string Kind, T? Before, T? After);        // Kind is "added", "updated" or "removed"

public class ValidationException(IReadOnlyList<string> errors) : Exception
{
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Errors { get; }                    // Message is the errors joined with "; "
}

public class Repository<T> where T : class, IEntity
{
    public event EventHandler<Change<T>>? Changed;
    public int Count { get; }
    public void AddRule(Func<T, string?> rule)                      // returns an error message, or null when fine
    public void Add(T item)
    public void Update(T item)
    public bool Remove(int id)
    public T? Find(int id)
    public IEnumerable<T> Where(Func<T, bool> predicate)            // lazy, in id order
    public IEnumerable<IReadOnlyList<T>> Pages(int size)            // in id order
    public Transaction BeginTransaction()

    public sealed class Transaction : IDisposable { public void Commit(); public void Dispose(); }
}
```

The tests use `public record Product(int Id, string Name, decimal Price) : IEntity;`, which is already in the starter.

**Rules**
- `Add` throws `InvalidOperationException("duplicate id <id>")` when the id is taken. `Update` throws `KeyNotFoundException("no item <id>")` for an unknown id. Both first run **every** rule and throw a `ValidationException` with all the error messages (in the order the rules were added) if any rule fails; nothing changes then.
- After a successful `Add`, `Update` or `Remove`, `Changed` is raised with the item before and after (`null` where there is none). `Remove` of an unknown id returns `false` and raises nothing.
- `Where` is lazy: it runs only when enumerated, and sees the items as they are then.
- `Pages(size)` gives lists of up to `size` items; `size` below 1 throws `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` **immediately**.
- **Transactions**: while a transaction is open, changes apply to the repository at once (so `Find` sees them), but `Changed` events are held back. `Commit` raises the held events in order. Disposing without committing **undoes** every change made since `BeginTransaction` and drops the held events. Only one transaction can be open at a time (`InvalidOperationException`); `Commit` after `Commit` or after `Dispose` throws `InvalidOperationException`; `Dispose` can be called more than once.

